{"skill":{"slug":"lnbits-with-qrcode","displayName":"LNBits Wallet wtih QR Code"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1770509935863,"changelog":"- Updated invoice QR code response: Change from using IMAGE: to MEDIA: followed by the file path, ensuring QR images are properly handled.\n- Adjusted expected QR file path for invoices from /tmp/lnbits_qr/ to ./.lnbits_qr/, standardizing location for QR code images.\n- Updated examples and instructions to align with new response format (MEDIA: and path on one line).\n- No changes to commands or protocol; only the output format and file paths for QR code delivery were updated.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3874,"sha256":"39bb653278b0dfaa2a32383e503e27fe800cd7db0f34eb5611b2b66d279dd008","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/lnbits_cli.py","size":7851,"sha256":"3ea6c9c2293e81fb04c077df37e4fe5e9012d5a055ea7a94ef5784e69cf27452","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3769,"sha256":"e37ed69dac02adf7f3b5c155b8cf8bd80eba371033a704567567845289a948c8","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2156,"sha256":"48f3f002192b0e66accbc2abd0b0ee08417144e37624b7b5b6735ae6d6f3cdaf","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789037684635,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4b9a43304835706b09b125ca611fc646fb463c6bb9071ceb206fa695dcaeaf2b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4b9a43304835706b09b125ca611fc646fb463c6bb9071ceb206fa695dcaeaf2b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: lnbits-with-qrcode\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill is designed to manage an LNbits Lightning Wallet and includes robust, explicit instructions in SKILL.md for the AI agent to follow critical safety protocols, such as never exposing secrets, requiring explicit user confirmation before making payments, and checking the balance first. The `scripts/lnbits_cli.py` script uses environment variables for API keys, communicates only with the specified LNbits API, and limits file system access to temporary QR code generation within the skill's working directory. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent; instead, the instructions actively guide the agent toward secure and responsible behavior.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161968340},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789037684635},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent LNbits wallet helper, but it can send real Lightning payments with only prompt-level confirmation and weak endpoint scoping for an admin key.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill uses LNBITS_API_KEY and LNBITS_BASE_URL as expected, but the script accepts the configured base URL without visible HTTPS/origin/redirect validation before sending the API key over the network.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation requires python3 and the qrcode[pil] package; no postinstall script or persistence mechanism was found, but the dependency is not version-pinned.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md instructs the assistant to check balance, decode, and ask Yes/No before paying, but scripts/lnbits_cli.py exposes a pay command that immediately posts an outgoing payment when invoked.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No cross-session service, hook, memory write, or privilege escalation was found; the main local side effect is QR PNG output under .lnbits_qr with best-effort cleanup of older files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The wallet-management purpose matches the balance, invoice, decode, QR, wallet creation, and pay capabilities, but outgoing Lightning payments and admin-key use are high-impact financial authority.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the assistant an LNbits admin key and you will supervise every payment. Use a dedicated wallet with limited funds, configure only a trusted HTTPS LNbits URL, avoid pasting secrets into chat, and treat payment approval prompts as mandatory because the CLI itself does not enforce confirmation.","findings":"[TT3] expected: Sending LNBITS_API_KEY to the configured LNbits API is expected for wallet operations, so this is not evidence of credential exfiltration by itself; the concern is endpoint validation rather than an unrelated data sink.\n[TP4] expected: Wallet creation, invoice decoding, and QR generation are disclosed in SKILL.md and README.md, although the frontmatter description is narrower than the full behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Paying invoices is central to the stated purpose, but the payment command has no built-in confirmation, dry-run, amount preview, limit, or approval token enforcement.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill handles an admin wallet key and financial transfers but does not define an enforceable narrow tool scope, endpoint scope, or file-write scope beyond natural-language instructions.\n[SDI-1] expected: Create-wallet and QR-file behavior is present in the user-facing usage sections, so those capabilities are not hidden in the artifact reviewed.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan concern is supported: BASE_URL is taken from the environment and used with urllib.request without visible scheme, origin, or redirect controls before authenticated requests.\n[T08] expected: The QR dependency is coherent with invoice QR generation, but the unpinned package leaves avoidable supply-chain exposure in a process that can access wallet credentials.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789037684635}}}}}